@MISC{temporaryCitekey-ynlcr,
  title    = "{Different forms of imbalance in strongly playable discrete games
              II: Multi-player RPS games}",
  author   = "Maimon, Itai",
  abstract = "Classic Rock-Paper-Scissors, RPS, has seen many variants and
              generalizations in the past several years. In the previous paper,
              we defined playability and balance for games. We used these
              definitions to show that different forms of imbalance agree on the
              most balanced and least balanced form of playable two-player
              n-object RPS games, referred to as (2,n)-RPS. We reintroduce these
