  journal   = "Foot and ankle clinics",
  publisher = "Elsevier BV",
  abstract  = "The Achilles tendon is the strongest and largest tendon in the
               body. It is the conjoined tendon of the gastrocnemius and the
               soleus muscles, and may have a small contribution from the
               plantaris. The muscles and the Achilles tendon are in the
